questions.question:
A JPA entity defines equality by its database id:

```java
@Entity
public class LineItem {
    @Id @GeneratedValue
    private Long id;
    private String sku;
    private int quantity;

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object o) {
        if (this == o) return true;
        if (!(o instanceof LineItem other)) return false;
        return Objects.equals(id, other.id);
    }

    @Override
    public int hashCode() {
        return Objects.hash(id);
    }
}
```

`Order` keeps its items in a `Set<LineItem>`. Two bugs reach production: when a customer adds two new items in the same request, only one is saved; and after an order has been saved, `order.getItems().remove(item)` silently does nothing, so deleted items come back. Explain both bugs and fix the entity.

questions.question_zh:
一个 JPA 实体用数据库 id 来定义相等性：

```java
@Entity
public class LineItem {
    @Id @GeneratedValue
    private Long id;
    private String sku;
    private int quantity;

    @Override
    public boolean equals(Object o) {
        if (this == o) return true;
        if (!(o instanceof LineItem other)) return false;
        return Objects.equals(id, other.id);
    }

    @Override
    public int hashCode() {
        return Objects.hash(id);
    }
}
```

`Order` 用一个 `Set<LineItem>` 保存订单明细。线上出现了两个 bug：顾客在同一个请求里添加两个新商品时，只有一个被保存；订单保存之后，`order.getItems().remove(item)` 悄无声息地什么都没做，于是被删除的明细又回来了。请解释这两个 bug 并修复这个实体。

questions.answer:
**Bug 1: all new entities are equal.** Before persisting, `id` is null for every new `LineItem`, and `Objects.equals(null, null)` is `true`. Both new items also have the same hash code, so the `HashSet` treats the second one as a duplicate and drops it.

**Bug 2: the hash code changes after insertion.** A `HashSet` files each element under the hash code it had when it was added. Saving the order assigns ids, which changes `hashCode()`. Later `contains` and `remove` look in the bucket for the new hash code, find nothing, and return `false`. The element is stranded in its old bucket: still iterated and still persisted, but unreachable by lookups.

**The rules this breaks.** Equal objects must have equal hash codes, and a hash code must not change while the object is in a hash-based collection. An id generated by the database breaks the second rule by design.

**Fix 1: id-based equality that is safe for new entities.**

```java
@Override
public boolean equals(Object o) {
    if (this == o) return true;
    if (!(o instanceof LineItem other)) return false;
    return id != null && id.equals(other.getId());
}

@Override
public int hashCode() {
    return LineItem.class.hashCode(); // constant: never changes
}
```

A new entity is equal only to itself, and the hash code never changes. All instances share one bucket, which is fine for the small collections entities usually live in, but don't use this for maps with millions of entries. Use `other.getId()` rather than `other.id`, so a Hibernate lazy proxy returns its real id, and `instanceof` rather than `getClass()`, because proxies are subclasses.

**Fix 2: an immutable business key.** If `(orderId, sku)` truly identifies a line and never changes, base `equals` and `hashCode` on it.

**Fix 3: assign the id up front.** Generate a UUID in the constructor, so the id exists before persisting and never changes. The cost is a larger, random primary key, so prefer a time-ordered UUID (version 7) to keep B-tree inserts mostly sequential.

**Related traps.** Lombok's `@Data` or `@EqualsAndHashCode` on an entity includes every field. That pulls in lazy collections, can trigger extra queries, and on bidirectional associations can recurse until `StackOverflowError`. Mutable keys break a `HashMap` in exactly the same way, so keep keys immutable; records are a good fit for value objects.

questions.answer_zh:
**Bug 1：所有新实体都相等。** 持久化之前，每个新 `LineItem` 的 `id` 都是 null，而 `Objects.equals(null, null)` 为 `true`。两个新明细的哈希值也相同，所以 `HashSet` 把第二个当成重复元素丢掉了。

**Bug 2：插入之后哈希值变了。** `HashSet` 按元素加入时的哈希值把它放进对应的桶。保存订单时分配了 id，`hashCode()` 随之改变。之后的 `contains` 和 `remove` 会去新哈希值对应的桶里找，什么也找不到，于是返回 `false`。这个元素被困在了旧桶里：遍历时还在，也仍然会被持久化，但通过查找永远找不到它。

**它违反了哪些规则。** 相等的对象必须有相等的哈希值，而且对象放在基于哈希的集合中时，哈希值不能改变。由数据库生成的 id 天生就违反了第二条规则。

**修复 1：对新实体也安全的、基于 id 的相等性。**

```java
@Override
public boolean equals(Object o) {
    if (this == o) return true;
    if (!(o instanceof LineItem other)) return false;
    return id != null && id.equals(other.getId());
}

@Override
public int hashCode() {
    return LineItem.class.hashCode(); // constant: never changes
}
```

新实体只与自身相等，而且哈希值永远不变。所有实例共用一个桶，这对实体通常所在的小集合来说没有问题，但不要把它用在有数百万条目的 map 上。使用 `other.getId()` 而不是 `other.id`，这样 Hibernate 的延迟加载代理会返回真实的 id；使用 `instanceof` 而不是 `getClass()`，因为代理是实体的子类。

**修复 2：使用不可变的业务键。** 如果 `(orderId, sku)` 确实能唯一标识一行明细且永不改变，就基于它来实现 `equals` 和 `hashCode`。

**修复 3：提前分配 id。** 在构造函数中生成 UUID，这样 id 在持久化之前就已存在，而且永不改变。代价是主键更大、更随机，所以优先使用按时间排序的 UUID（version 7），让 B 树的插入基本保持顺序。

**相关的陷阱。** 在实体上使用 Lombok 的 `@Data` 或 `@EqualsAndHashCode` 会把所有字段都包含进来。这会牵扯到延迟加载的集合，可能触发额外的查询，在双向关联上还可能无限递归，直到 `StackOverflowError`。可变的 key 会以完全相同的方式破坏 `HashMap`，所以 key 要保持不可变；record 很适合用来做值对象。
